/-!
# The ATLAS permutation model of the Higman--Sims group

`TauCeti.Sporadic.HS` is the subgroup of permutations of `Fin 100` generated by the image tables
in the ATLAS files `HSG1-p100B0.m1` and `HSG1-p100B0.m2`. File point `i` is Lean point `i - 1`;
the tables specify images, not preimages. The permutations have computable bodies so that later
order and stabilizer calculations can use this exact model.

The ATLAS presentation `HSG1-P1` uses left-to-right products, whereas Mathlib composes functions
right to left. Sending the presentation generators to the inverses of the file generators
satisfies all thirteen transcribed relators. These images generate the model, giving a surjection
from `TauCeti.SporadicName.HS.Group` and proving that the presented group is nontrivial. No order,
finiteness, or simplicity of the presented group is asserted.

## References

* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, representation `HSG1-p100B0`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/permrep/HSG1-p100B0>.
  Generator image files:
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/HS/mtx/HSG1-p100B0.m1> and
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/spor/HS/mtx/HSG1-p100B0.m2>.
* J. N. Bray, ATLAS presentation `HSG1-P1`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/pres/HSG1-P1>, transcribed in
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.hsPresentation`.
-/

public section

open scoped commutatorElement

namespace TauCeti.Sporadic

namespace HS

